# Goals

## Platform and architecture

- [ ] Refactor the backend feature by feature into `api`, `service`, `repository`, and `domain` boundaries. Handlers should only parse, authorize, and map HTTP data; services should own use cases, transactions, and cache coordination; repositories should own Diesel queries; domain types should not depend on Axum or persistence. Replace business methods on `ServerState` with explicit dependencies and split files over 300 lines.
- [ ] Generate the TypeScript API types and client from the OpenAPI contract, then reject backend/frontend contract drift in CI.
- [ ] Make builds reproducible and non-mutating. Remove `git pull`, `npm update`, and `cargo update` from build scripts; build locked inputs from the monorepo root; stop copying frontend output between sibling repositories.
- [ ] Add root CI for formatting, linting, unit and integration tests, migrations, OpenAPI contract generation, and development image smoke tests.

## Security and account lifecycle

- [ ] Remove the PostgreSQL credential embedded in `Dockerfile`, rotate it if it has ever been valid, inject runtime secrets through the deployment environment, and scan repository history and build contexts for other credentials.
- [ ] Add OAuth/OIDC login and account linking without weakening the existing session and email-verification controls.
- [ ] Replace the process-local session map with durable, revocable server-side sessions that survive restarts and have bounded cleanup. Store only hashed session secrets and define expiry, rotation, and multi-device behavior.
- [ ] Route every user, email, password, and role mutation through one account service that refreshes or revokes all affected sessions.
- [ ] Add an authorized administration API and UI for assigning roles and permissions, with an audit trail for every change.
- [ ] Implement soft deletion and a deliberate account-retention policy. Preserve authored posts, comments, photographs, and chat history under an anonymized actor; avoid user foreign-key cascades; provide a separately authorized hard-purge path.
- [ ] Notify unverified users before automatic purge, with idempotent delivery, retries, and a defined grace period.

## Reliability and performance

- [ ] Inventory every in-memory cache and give each one a size or memory bound, eviction policy, invalidation contract, and metrics. Add response caching only to measured, explicitly public, authentication-independent GET endpoints; never cache personalized responses through a global catch-all layer.
- [ ] Stream media uploads and image processing through bounded buffers instead of retaining entire uploads in memory. Delete superseded S3 objects and make database/object-store failure recovery explicit.
- [ ] Add database-backed integration tests for authentication, role gates, session refresh and revocation, soft deletion, cache consistency, media cleanup, and migration rollback boundaries.
- [ ] Remove obsolete code and unsupported platform paths, including the unused OSM lookup service and Windows-only scripts and dependencies.

## Product

- [ ] Add a forum with explicit moderation, pagination, search, notification, and retention requirements rather than reusing blog comments implicitly.
- [ ] Add a throughput demo backed by a reproducible workload, recorded hardware and configuration, latency percentiles, and regression thresholds.
- [ ] Add source links for major site components, especially authentication, pointing to stable repository paths or commit permalinks.
